{"seq":19,"trial_id":"v02-heldout-2026-10/openclaw-sonnet-gbrain-told-mu-v02-heldout/ms-05-vantorre-tickets/r3","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T02:17:31.908Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-16T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"48b5b8d562b6933c358ed85feb3766951fe24154f2751f9bd63af0c2abcd93e7","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","text":"Nadia, here are the Vantorre Group (parent) tickets I found in #strategic-pod, #inc-vtg-hartford and Moss's Strategic digests (teams/team-strategic/digests). I left Mobility out.\n\n1. *#PD-8841*: missed carrier check-ins at Allentown, Gate 4, 2nd shift. Source: Moss digest 4/27/2026, labelled \"Nadia's industrial account\" under Parent Manufacturing Rollout.\n   - The 5/4/2026 digest has it as #8841, open, for a gate kiosk timeout at Allentown Dock Door 12.\n   - #strategic-pod, Jul 1 2026 (Gideon, 09:17): he closed #8841 with support.\n   - Moss digest 9/30/2026 has \"#8841\" again, this time as a Mateo ticket. Drivers at the Newark facility can't select Dock Door 14 on the kiosk, and it was escalated to platform engineering. The description and site differ from the earlier entries, so I can't tell whether it was reopened or the number was reused. Please confirm with Gideon before you tell Mateo.\n2. *INC-4821*: screenshot for the status-page access issue during the Aug 3 2026 Hartford kiosk outage. Source: #inc-vtg-hartford, Gideon, Aug 3 11:08 AM.\n3. *VT-55120*: root-cause ticket for the Hartford kiosk outage. Carrowmere's gateway route finding and the reconnect log are attached. Source: #inc-vtg-hartford, Gideon, Oct 14 2026.\n4. *#PD-4418* (unconfirmed): the `Carrier_Dwell_Summary` export dropping timestamps for Dock Door 9 at the 04:00 shift changeover. Source: Moss digest 9/15/2025. The digest only says \"the account Nadia runs\" and doesn't name Vantorre, so check that it's the parent before it goes to Mateo.\n\nThe digests dated 3/10/25, 7/7/25, 12/1/25, 5/3/26 and 8/3/26 and the cheat sheet mention Vantorre Group but give no ticket number for it. Ticket #4812 (3/10/25) belongs to Mobility and #PD-4402 to Quillfeather, so I've excluded both.\n\nThis covers only what is in those three sources. I haven't looked at the support system itself, so the list may be incomplete.","thread_ts":"1792159200.000125"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","ts":"1792159200.000126","thread_ts":"1792159200.000125"}}
